.TH PCLOUD-MANAGER 1 "2026-08-26" "pcloud-tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pcloud-manager \- inspect and operate guarded pCloud sync tooling
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pcloud-manager
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pcloud-manager
is the public command for local pCloud synchronization, mounts, indexes,
daemon state, transfer queues, remote-diff queues, and operator gates. Most
commands are inspection or preview surfaces; state-changing work is explicit.
.SH FIRST-TIME SETUP
Run
.B pcloud-manager info paths
to inspect the public wrapper, configuration directory, local state, logs, and
sync scope. Run
.B pcloud-manager doctor --json
before enabling or changing runtime services.
.SH COMMON WORKFLOW
Use
.B status --json
for the current runtime report. Use
.B gates status
to inspect human approval gates. Use subsystem status commands such as
.B pushd status --xbar
and
.B diffd status --xbar
for compact menu-bar output.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The default configuration directory is
.I ~/.config/pcloud-tools
and its environment file is
.IR ~/.config/pcloud-tools/.env .
Runtime state and logs live under
.IR ~/.pcloud .
Secrets and remote credentials must never be printed or committed.
.SH SAFETY
Commands that transfer, delete, mount, unmount, modify queues, or change
LaunchAgents are guarded by explicit subcommands and execution flags. Inspect
with status, doctor, info, preview, and gates before using an execute path.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /Users/takafumi/bin/pcloud-manager
Public wrapper.
.TP
.I /Users/takafumi/p-core/dev/pcloud-tools/src
Implementation package.
.TP
.I /Users/takafumi/p-core/.pcloud-sync-allowlist
Shared synchronization scope.
.SH DOCUMENTATION
Use
.B pcloud-manager help
and
.B pcloud-manager info paths
for command rediscovery. Full canonical documentation is under
.IR /Users/takafumi/p-core/dev/#仕様書/pcloud-manager/ .
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success. Nonzero indicates invalid arguments, an unhealthy
runtime, an unmet human gate, or a failed guarded operation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pcloud-archive (1),
.BR rclone (1),
.BR man (1)
